From ed7a0131638c5b8c883838fcf0a375bdc4a6a509 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 07:50:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add an optional Caddy log output directory setting, separate
 from Caddy Manager's own logs directory

Adds Settings > Caddy Settings > Logging > "Caddy log output directory":
an optional override for the directory written into a block's `output
file` line, i.e. where Caddy itself will actually write that block's
access log. It's independent from the existing Logs directory path
(Directories tab), which is only where Caddy Manager looks to list,
tail, and delete log files -- the two default to the same place but can
now be pointed at different filesystem paths, for setups where Caddy
and Caddy Manager don't share the same view of the logs volume (e.g.
separate containers). Leaving it blank keeps current behavior exactly
as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GdhKf193j6ggwAGFYCUaJg
